{
  "mn90:0.1": "Middle Discourses 90 ",
  "mn90:0.2": "At Kaṇṇakatthala ",
  "mn90:1.1": "So I have heard. ",
  "mn90:1.2": "At one time the Buddha was staying near Ujuññā in the deer park at Kaṇṇakatthala. ",
  "mn90:2.1": "Now at that time King Pasenadi of Kosala had arrived at Ujuññā on some business. ",
  "mn90:2.2": "Then he addressed a man, ",
  "mn90:2.3": "“Please, my man, go to the Buddha, and in my name bow with your head to his feet. Ask him if he is healthy and well, nimble, strong, and living comfortably. ",
  "mn90:2.4": "",
  "mn90:2.5": "And then say: ",
  "mn90:2.6": "‘Sir, King Pasenadi of Kosala will come to see you today when he has finished breakfast.’” ",
  "mn90:2.7": "“Yes, Your Majesty,” that man replied. He did as the king asked. ",
  "mn90:2.8": "",
  "mn90:2.9": "",
  "mn90:2.10": "",
  "mn90:3.1": "The sisters Somā and Sakulā heard this. ",
  "mn90:3.2": "",
  "mn90:3.3": "While the meal was being served, they approached the king and said, ",
  "mn90:3.4": "“Great king, since you are going to the Buddha, please bow in our name with your head to his feet. Ask him if he is healthy and well, nimble, strong, and living comfortably.” ",
  "mn90:3.5": "",
  "mn90:4.1": "When he had finished breakfast, King Pasenadi went to the Buddha, bowed, sat down to one side, and said to him, ",
  "mn90:4.2": "“Sir, the sisters Somā and Sakulā bow with their heads to your feet. They ask if you are healthy and well, nimble, strong, and living comfortably.” ",
  "m